  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1293",
      "html": "<p>Rineloricaria platyura (Müller &amp; Troschel, 1849). Common names: Pearlscale Whiptail, Amazonia Whiptail. Type locality: Rupununi River, Guyana. Size: 14 cm SL. IUCN: Least Concern.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1293",
      "html": "<p>South America: various coastal rivers from near the Amazon mouth to the Essequibo River, including the lower and middle Amazon, Madeira, Canumã, Acari, Orapu, Comté, Mana and Rupununi.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1293",
      "html": "<p>The fish should be provided with half-pipe type refuges, which are also often used as spawning sites.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1293",
      "html": "<p>Adaptable omnivores, these fish will eat most foods, from cucumber or zucchini slices to frozen bloodworm or dry flake foods.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1293",
      "html": "<p>Peaceful and not territorial.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1293",
      "html": "<p>Males grow short spines on the top of the head and on the pectoral fins.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1293",
      "html": "<p>Like many Rineloricaria, this species spawns in open-ended tubes, although at least one report also confirmed spawning on glass. There is no breeding report.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "references",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1293",
      "html": "<p>Reisen in Britisch-Guiana, pp 631.</p>"
    }
  ],
